# 17 one-base peaks: promoter=1, exon=5, intron=4, downstream=6, intergenic=1.
# Three wide peaks have centres 250 (promoter), 425 (intron), 10 (exon).
# Centre totals with 100bp downstream: promoter=2, exon=6, intron=5,
# downstream=6, intergenic=1. Off: downstream's 6 become intergenic.
# Wide peak bp: [190,310) = exon 19 + promoter 1 + intron 50 + downstream 50;
# [390,460) = downstream 10 + exon 20 + intron 40;
# E [0,20) = downstream 10 + exon 9 + promoter 1.
# Add the 17 single bases: promoter=3, exon=53, intron=94, downstream=76,
# intergenic=1; total 227. No UTRs. At window 10 only centre 249 changes
# from downstream to intergenic (centre downstream=5, intergenic=2).
